**Computing the area of hexagon $A_5A_6B_5B_6C_5C_6$** via the Shoelace formula with vertices:
$$A_5(61,81),\; A_6(-59,61),\; B_5(-79,13),\; B_6(-19,-82),\; C_5(37,-82),\; C_6(97,33).$$

$$\text{Area} = \tfrac{1}{2}\left|\sum_{i} (x_i\, y_{i+1} - x_{i+1}\, y_i)\right|$$

| Edge | $x_i y_{i+1} - x_{i+1} y_i$ |
|------|---------------------------|
| $A_5\to A_6$ | $61\cdot61 - (-59)\cdot81 = 3721+4779 = 8500$ |
| $A_6\to B_5$ | $(-59)\cdot13 - (-79)\cdot61 = -767+4819 = 4052$ |
| $B_5\to B_6$ | $(-79)\cdot(-82) - (-19)\cdot13 = 6478+247 = 6725$ |
| $B_6\to C_5$ | $(-19)\cdot(-82) - 37\cdot(-82) = 1558+3034 = 4592$ |
| $C_5\to C_6$ | $37\cdot33 - 97\cdot(-82) = 1221+7954 = 9175$ |
| $C_6\to A_5$ | $97\cdot81 - 61\cdot33 = 7857-2013 = 5844$ |

$$\text{Sum} = 8500+4052+6725+4592+9175+5844 = 38888$$

$$\text{Area} = \frac{38888}{2} = \boxed{19444}$$

